$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical Procedure for Pd-catalyzed Arylation
of Chloroacetonitrile with Arylboronic Acids. (Table 1, entry 1) A 10-mL
sealable glass vessel containing a magnetic stirring bar was flame-dried
under vacuum and filled with argon after cooling to room temperature. To
the glass vessel were added Pd(OAc)2 (1.7 mg, 7.5 μmol), SPhos (6.2 mg,
15 μmol), and dry dioxane (450 μL) at room temperature under a stream of
argon. After stirring the mixture at this temperature for 30 min,
chloroacetonitrile (19.0 μL, 0.3 mmol), phenylboronic acid 1a (54.9 mg,
0.45 mmol), Na2CO3 (47.7 mg, 0.45 mmol), dry dioxane (450 μL) and H2O (90
μL) were added, and then the vessel was sealed. The mixture was stirred
at 60 °C for 12 h. After cooling to room temperature, the mixture was
passed through a pad of silica gel with copious washings with EtOAc (~15
mL). The filtrate was concentrated under reduced pressure. The crude
product was purified by PTLC (EtOAc/hexane = 1:20).
4-Fluorophenylacetonitrile (2d)2 Table 1, entry 4: Purification by PTLC
(EtOAc/hexane = 1:20). 32.4 mg, 80% isolated yield; colorless oil. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3) δ 3.73 (s, 2H), 7.04-7.10 (m, 2H), 7.28-7.33 (m, 2H).
13C NMR (100 MHz, CDCl3) δ 22.9, 116.1 (d, J = 22 Hz), 117.7, 125.6,
129.6 (d, J = 8.6 Hz), 162.4 (d, J = 248 Hz). HRMS (DART) m/z calcd for
C8H6NF [M]+: 135.0484, found 135.0484.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed vessel used, Suzuki-Miyaura cross-coupling reaction
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM The Concise Synthesis of Unsymmetric Triarylacetonitriles via
Pd-Catalyzed Sequential Arylation: A New Synthetic Approach to Tri- and
Tetraarylmethanes
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Nambo, Masakazu; Yar, Muhammad; Smith, Joel D.; Crudden, Cathleen M.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organic Letters (2015), 17(1), 50-53

