$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: A solution of 2,4-dichloropyrimidine (575 mg,
3.86 mmol), 4-chlorophenylboronic acid (600 mg, 3.86 mmol), 2N Na2CO3
(3.86 mL, 7.72 mmol) and Pd(PPh3)4 (45 mg, 0.039 mmol) in acetonitrile
(13 mL) was heated to 90°C for 4 h and monitored by TLC. After cooling to
room temperature, the mixture was poured into water (30mL), and extracted
with EtOAc (50 mL x 2). The combined organic phases were dried over
anhydrous MgSO4,filtered and concentrated in vacuo. After removal of the
solvent, the residue was purified by flash chromatography
(ethylacetate/n-hexane) on silica gel.
2-chloro-4-(4-chlorophenyl)pyrimidine (669 mg, 77% yield). A mixture of
this intermediate (100 mg, 0.444 mmol), 4-aminobenzenesulfonamide (76 mg,
0.444 mmol) and catalytic amount of 1N HCl (a few drops) in ethanol (2
mL) was heated for 2 h at 160°C under microwave irradiation. After
cooling and evaporation of the mixture, the resulting solid was washed
with methanol (10 mL), The product as white solid (105 mg, 66% yield).
4-((4-(4-chlorophenyl)pyrimidin-2-yl)amino)benzenesulfonamide (18).
4-((4-(4-(4-fluorophenoxy)phenyl)pyrimidin-2-yl)amino)benzenesulfonamide
(24). Compound 24 was prepared (11 mg, 2 steps-6% overall yield)
according to GP I from (4-(4-fluorophenoxy)phenyl)boronic acid instead of
4-chlorophenylboronic acid as a starting material. The condition of
Suzuki Coupling was identical to compound 21. 1H NMR (500MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ
10.08 (s, 1H), 8.59 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 1H), 8.22 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.99
(d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.76 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H), 7.47 (d, J = 5.2 Hz, 1H),
7.31-7.28 (m, 2H), 7.21-7.18 (m, 4H), 7.12 (d, J = 8.8 Hz, 2H). 13C NMR
(100MHz, DMSO-d6 ) δ 163.0, 159.9, 159.7, 159.0, 157.5, 151.6, 151.5,
143.7, 136.1, 131.1, 129.0, 126.6, 121.7, 121.7, 117.9, 117.7, 116.9,
116.7, 108.5. HRMS (EI+) m/zcalcd for C22H17FN4O3S [M + Na]+, 459.0898;
found, 459.0908.
